<title>UK: UK farmers urge selective cull to proceed quickly.</title>
<headline>UK farmers urge selective cull to proceed quickly.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leaders of UK farmers' unions urged the government Wednesday to proceed with a selective cull in the UK cattle herd to pave the way for lifting the worldwide ban on British beef.</p>
<p>&quot;We urge the government to introduce immediately the necessary Statutory Instruments to allow the immediate implementation of the selective cull...so that the UK can, at last, fulfil the pledges made by the Prime Minister in Florence,&quot; said a joint statement by the leaders of main farm unions, including the National Farmers Union (NFU).</p>
<p>The selective cull was one of the five obligations undertaken by the UK at a key meeting in Florence in June to lift the ban slammed after the BSE (Bovine Spongiform Encephalopathy) scare on British beef.</p>
<p>--Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
